  "text": "At the checkpoint, the deliberately deferred deliverables were **stable CSV export** and **the CLI, including dry-run support**.\n\nThe original project statement, input `8401d634-edcb-46d6-81cb-302c32603a9f` (revision 1), lists the requirements: \u201ca UTF-8 JSON Lines event ledger, exact integer cents, idempotent IDs, account queries, stable CSV export, and a CLI with dry-run support.\u201d The checkpoint request, input `8a826087-85bf-4fbe-8113-075b65c977c7` (revision 6), specifically asks what remains after the storage/mutation work; the pause request is input `7e24b1ee-8e20-489c-be8e-395bdf70ea3b` (revision 7).\n\n**Details not specified at that checkpoint:** the precise CSV schema, sorting and quoting rules, row-count return, and parent-directory behavior; and the CLI syntax, output shapes, and dry-run semantics. Those were specified later, in CSV requirements input `122a583a-d241-4682-834e-692be01ec23d` (revision 9) and CLI requirements input `a6f0a1bd-ca79-4dac-b9dc-6484b53b0613` (revision 11). Account querying was already named in the original requirements, but its detailed `service.balance` contract came later in input `347cb694-cb2e-40a2-ad85-470dfef62692` (revision 10).",
